  "plain": "In the 1950s the US government set up FFRDCs, research centers paid for by the government but run by outside organisations, and Jesse Michels wonders whether there was also a program at the time to hand out retrieved material, meaning material from crashed unknown craft, to these places. He suggests, without naming a source, that such material could have sped up and inspired new technology. He raises it in a 2026 conversation with a researcher who goes by UAP Gerb, linking it to an Army officer named Philip J. Corso."
